WEBVTT

00:02.580 --> 00:05.830
It's the petrification device and an
infinite supply of rejuvenation fluid!

00:05.830 --> 00:09.540
Petrify someone and revive them,
and you heal any injury, no matter how bad!

00:09.540 --> 00:11.940
It's the Dr. Stone set!

00:13.450 --> 00:15.000
Does that mean...

00:16.260 --> 00:18.500
Finally... He'll finally...

00:20.800 --> 00:22.030
Yeah.

00:22.450 --> 00:25.500
Let's get him out of cold sleep.

00:26.530 --> 00:29.690
The strongest high school primate...

00:29.690 --> 00:32.110
Shishio Tsukasa!

02:11.100 --> 02:12.470
Finally...

02:13.200 --> 02:15.010
Finally, Nii-san...

02:15.800 --> 02:17.730
Although it's still a gamble.

02:17.730 --> 02:20.150
We only get one shot, 
and there's no other way.

02:20.150 --> 02:24.910
We say "cold sleep," 
but really, we just froze him...

02:26.030 --> 02:28.210
That's not the real problem, though, is it?

02:28.210 --> 02:30.290
You can always trust a sailor's gut.

02:31.550 --> 02:33.290
When Ibara jabbed you...

02:36.300 --> 02:39.310
Senku, given how pragmatic as you are,

02:39.310 --> 02:42.260
you would have healed yourself 
immediately with the Dr. Stone set.

02:42.260 --> 02:43.230
Am I right?

02:44.050 --> 02:46.720
Yet the crack in your 
forehead is still there.

02:46.720 --> 02:48.490
In other words, you didn't use it.

02:48.490 --> 02:51.130
You saved it for Tsukasa.

02:51.130 --> 02:52.100
Why?

02:52.100 --> 02:53.940
The only reason I can think of...

02:54.160 --> 02:55.350
Yup.

02:55.350 --> 02:58.400
The petrification device is out of battery.

02:59.230 --> 03:01.280
That thing runs on batteries?!

03:02.410 --> 03:03.910
Dunno.

03:03.910 --> 03:08.150
And we don't exactly have the luxury of 
smashing it open to have a look-see inside.

03:08.590 --> 03:10.760
But it's using some kind of energy.

03:10.760 --> 03:14.710
The one thing that could never happen 
is for it to make energy out of nothing.

03:15.220 --> 03:16.050
Kirisame...

03:16.750 --> 03:19.880
Is the petrification beam's 
area specified in radii?

03:21.020 --> 03:22.390
Yes, why?

03:22.710 --> 03:26.560
When I stoned Ibara, I specified five meters.

03:27.150 --> 03:32.350
But the petrification beam barely 
made maybe a meter and a half.

03:32.560 --> 03:34.080
That's impossible!

03:34.080 --> 03:36.980
It's never deviated in size.

03:38.220 --> 03:40.110
Listen well, kids.

03:40.570 --> 03:45.470
You must never use the petrification 
beam over a wide area.

03:47.400 --> 03:48.930
It's out of energy?

04:05.860 --> 04:07.460
Get away from there!

04:07.460 --> 04:09.410
Mirai! Tsukasa!

04:12.140 --> 04:15.440
The only way to save you 
will be to petrify you.

04:16.850 --> 04:18.270
Petrify him to save him?!

04:19.160 --> 04:23.000
We're going to exploit the 
regenerative effects of

04:23.000 --> 04:25.530
coming out of petrification to heal him.

04:37.370 --> 04:39.290
Just work for a moment, please...

04:39.640 --> 04:44.130
We just need it to shine one last time.

04:52.960 --> 04:57.150
Mirai, hold your brother's 
hand with all you've got.

04:57.540 --> 04:58.770
I see!

04:58.770 --> 05:00.940
If you hold him really close to the device,

05:00.940 --> 05:03.950
it might give him just a 
little more of the light.

05:03.950 --> 05:06.500
That's seriously not going 
to make a difference.

05:07.370 --> 05:09.910
You're gonna crush Mirai-chan's hand!

05:10.960 --> 05:13.980
I don't care if my hand gets crushed.

05:13.980 --> 05:17.170
If that gives Nii-san a better 
chance of coming back...

05:17.960 --> 05:20.420
Guess it's better to do it than not.

05:21.880 --> 05:26.630
And if I get caught in the beam, 
it'll heal my wounds and cracks, too. Perfect.

05:27.840 --> 05:32.940
You know how phones and shavers 
will work for a brief second

05:32.940 --> 05:36.100
after the battery's dead if you 
turn them off and back on?

05:44.590 --> 05:47.770
One meter, one second.

05:56.190 --> 05:57.660
Revival fluid!

06:24.120 --> 06:26.900
Nii-san!

06:29.550 --> 06:32.570
Look at that. What a moving reunion.

06:33.200 --> 06:35.140
Aren't you going? You're the Tsukasa fan.

06:35.140 --> 06:38.610
I want to, of course, but family comes first.

06:38.610 --> 06:41.770
I have to know my place.

06:43.350 --> 06:45.650
I never knew you were so strong, Ruri.

06:45.650 --> 06:46.370
Yeah.

06:46.370 --> 06:49.930
We've gotten used to her being sickly, 
but she's Gorilla Kohaku's big sis, remember.

06:52.840 --> 06:56.640
Welcome back, Tsuka-san!

07:11.290 --> 07:12.360
What's the situation?

07:12.650 --> 07:14.260
He only just woke up.

07:14.260 --> 07:17.260
That's how Tsukasa always is.

07:17.260 --> 07:20.080
I don't think he ever loses his cool.

07:21.080 --> 07:22.800
We're attacking the Moon!

07:26.740 --> 07:29.810
H-He definitely lost his cool a bit.

07:29.810 --> 07:31.950
I mean, can you blame him?

07:31.950 --> 07:34.800
Especially if you tell a moderner 
that we're going to the Moon.

07:36.500 --> 07:38.860
We can only take a few people to the Moon.

07:38.860 --> 07:41.360
You'll need a strong fighter.

07:41.360 --> 07:44.400
I assume that's the reason you revived me.

07:45.830 --> 07:48.480
That's right. Ten billion percent.

07:48.480 --> 07:50.280
You seem to get it.

07:50.280 --> 07:54.070
I wouldn't want to see any more 
of your damn face otherwise.

07:57.120 --> 07:59.950
Senku! I just figured it out!

07:59.950 --> 08:02.730
You hurried back for Tsukasa's sake

08:02.730 --> 08:06.370
because you were worried he was 
going to spoil in the freezer, right?

08:06.810 --> 08:10.340
I know you both hate all 
that mushy stuff, though!

08:07.170 --> 08:10.460
Carried Away Level: Max

08:10.340 --> 08:13.510
H-He's absolutely tactless.

08:10.460 --> 08:13.750
Carried Away Level: Max

08:13.510 --> 08:15.240
Ginro, you...

08:15.240 --> 08:19.170
Well, if he just wanted someone super 
strong, he could've taken my top student—

08:19.170 --> 08:22.140
I mean, guard, Matsukaze-kun.

08:23.560 --> 08:25.150
<i>So that man is Tsukasa...</i>

08:25.440 --> 08:26.970
<i>I can tell with one look.</i>

08:26.970 --> 08:30.660
<i>He's a warrior of impressive presence, 
his body trained to the absolute limit.</i>

08:32.100 --> 08:33.650
My name is Matsukaze.

08:33.860 --> 08:36.100
Tsukasa-dono, if it would be all right,

08:36.100 --> 08:39.410
I would like to challenge 
you once you are well.

08:40.460 --> 08:41.640
I wouldn't mind.

08:41.640 --> 08:43.080
Immediately, if you'd like.

08:43.770 --> 08:45.650
Why don't we go outside?

08:53.910 --> 08:54.840
I am defeated.

08:56.550 --> 08:58.800
Carried Away Level: 0

08:59.600 --> 09:00.500
<i>He's strong.</i>

09:01.180 --> 09:04.310
<i>If he were to learn modern martial arts...</i>

09:04.310 --> 09:09.120
Dude, Tsukasa's completely back 
to normal. This can't be good.

09:09.120 --> 09:12.880
If he ever starts saying any nasty shit 
about killing Senku or anything...

09:12.880 --> 09:15.840
Officer Yo-kun here's gonna 
stop him with his gun!

09:15.840 --> 09:18.180
Your hand's shaking, though.

09:19.450 --> 09:20.330
Matsukaze...

09:20.330 --> 09:25.960
Restaurant
Francois

09:21.110 --> 09:23.240
He's just as capable a man himself.

09:26.970 --> 09:31.530
I can't shamelessly join the Kingdom 
of Science now to serve as a warrior.

09:32.250 --> 09:36.670
The fact remains that I've destroyed 
statues for the sake of a different ide—

09:36.670 --> 09:39.010
Yeah, yeah, I don't care.

09:39.010 --> 09:42.210
You really aren't interested 
in that kind of stuff, are you?

09:42.210 --> 09:45.480
And Yuzuriha ended up 
repairing all of them, anyway.

09:45.790 --> 09:50.090
We can deal with that boring 
crap until we both go bald later.

09:50.090 --> 09:53.030
If we don't act now, 
they're going to wipe out humanity.

09:53.370 --> 10:00.620
Since the device is out of battery, 
Senku's crack will never go away now.

10:01.820 --> 10:04.870
Yeah, I don't give a rat's ass.

10:05.150 --> 10:08.280
If we defeat Why-Man and learn the 
secrets of the petrification beam,

10:08.280 --> 10:10.740
he can use Dr. Stone to 
heal himself all he wants.

10:10.740 --> 10:13.410
Why should Senku-chan get all the fun?

10:15.260 --> 10:16.480
Me, too.

10:16.480 --> 10:17.920
War paint.

10:17.920 --> 10:20.970
Huh? Why are you drawing that on?

10:21.270 --> 10:24.350
Perfect symbolism, don't you think?

10:25.140 --> 10:31.150
Our war paint stays on until the very moment 
we defeat the source of the petrification.

10:34.650 --> 10:36.150
Me, too!

10:36.150 --> 10:37.840
Here I go!

10:37.840 --> 10:40.370
That looks nothing like how it used to.

10:46.040 --> 10:48.750
What about you, Tsukasa-chan?

10:48.750 --> 10:53.470
Or do you not like having 
scribbles on your pristine skin?

10:53.470 --> 10:55.350
<i>How could he refuse?</i>

10:53.470 --> 10:58.670
Well? What do you think? 
Wouldn't a heart look nice? Well? Well?

10:55.350 --> 10:56.900
<i>It would be awkward.</i>

10:57.210 --> 10:58.670
<i>Amazing.</i>

11:01.530 --> 11:04.580
Thank you, Gen and everyone.

11:07.470 --> 11:09.980
m 0 0 l 208 0 l 208 80 l 0 80

11:07.470 --> 11:09.980
Shishio Tsukasa
joined the party!!

11:15.560 --> 11:21.530
Finally! Tsukasa is a member 
of the Kingdom of Science!

11:22.410 --> 11:25.950
Now we can take on Why-Man easy, right?

11:26.200 --> 11:30.540
All right, it's time to go attack the Moon!

11:31.770 --> 11:37.890
To fight Why-Man, we're going to have to 
collect a ridiculous amount of resources

11:37.890 --> 11:40.970
that are ten billion percent 
impossible to find in Japan.

11:41.220 --> 11:43.650
A world exploration party, huh?

11:43.650 --> 11:46.890
If only we had a professional explorer...

11:46.890 --> 11:49.110
Do you know who I am?!

11:49.110 --> 11:51.230
I'm the king of materials! I got this!

11:51.570 --> 11:55.820
I'll go find all the rare materials we need!

11:55.820 --> 11:58.450
You really are a simpleton, aren't you?

11:58.450 --> 12:00.990
I'm gonna help, too!

12:01.390 --> 12:02.700
All right, then.

12:03.030 --> 12:05.130
Let's get ready to set out!

12:05.610 --> 12:06.580
Yeah!

12:06.580 --> 12:07.390
Let's do this!

12:09.340 --> 12:10.080
Gen.

12:10.410 --> 12:12.000
When you betrayed me...

12:13.750 --> 12:19.220
I thought my biggest mistake 
was reviving you.

12:21.770 --> 12:25.080
But I'm really glad you're here.

12:31.730 --> 12:35.630
Well, you know, I can't really 
do anything on my own.

12:35.940 --> 12:40.400
I'm just a bat bastard who tries 
to get people to do things for me.

12:40.810 --> 12:44.150
There's very little that 
anyone can do on their own.

12:45.220 --> 12:48.160
Am I supposed to be convinced of that 
by <i>you</i>? You can do anything yourself.

12:48.510 --> 12:52.540
Is it not important to be able to 
bring people's abilities together?

12:56.970 --> 12:59.150
Damn, it smells so good!

12:59.150 --> 13:02.900
Look at all that long-lasting stollen bread!

13:03.750 --> 13:06.470
Our next voyage is going to 
take us all over the world.

13:06.470 --> 13:09.810
It's a whole different scale. 
It'll take at least a few months!

13:09.810 --> 13:11.940
We'll need plenty of supplies, too.

13:11.940 --> 13:13.380
Let's get them all packed in!

13:13.380 --> 13:15.390
We gotta head out ASAP!

13:16.420 --> 13:17.940
What are you talking about?

13:18.150 --> 13:20.230
Why are we in such a hurry?

13:20.230 --> 13:22.190
We finally <i>just</i> got back!

13:22.670 --> 13:25.580
Because it's going to be cold 
once it's winter? Is that it?

13:27.630 --> 13:32.410
He says he wants a model of this 
spaceship road map immediately...

13:32.410 --> 13:33.930
Road map?

13:33.930 --> 13:36.410
It looks a bit different from the usual...

13:36.650 --> 13:40.490
Yeah, I just need you to bang out 
something quick and dirty in 3D.

13:41.020 --> 13:44.170
Quick and dirty, huh?

13:44.170 --> 13:46.450
You know, I don't think Senku-kun understands

13:46.450 --> 13:51.100
what it means to be someone who 
makes stuff. Right, Kaseki-sensei?

13:51.100 --> 13:53.610
I get it. I totally get it.

13:53.610 --> 13:56.310
I hate when people say that.

13:56.310 --> 13:59.440
We're gonna have to show him!

14:06.380 --> 14:11.670
We've finished the spaceship road map!

14:12.610 --> 14:15.630
Fast as always, maker duo.

14:16.150 --> 14:17.370
What is this?

14:17.620 --> 14:19.880
The road map is in here?

14:24.880 --> 14:26.070
Whoa...

14:26.070 --> 14:27.120
Damn...

14:27.120 --> 14:28.130
Awesome...

14:28.130 --> 14:30.890
This is... the spaceship...

14:32.120 --> 14:34.970
...road map?

14:38.100 --> 14:40.060
m 0 0 l 198 0 l 198 80 l 0 80

14:38.100 --> 14:40.060
Globe
acquired!!

14:38.250 --> 14:40.060
Globe acquired!!

14:42.610 --> 14:44.750
You guys took it way too far.

14:46.010 --> 14:48.540
I'm starting to get hooked 
on building models!

14:48.540 --> 14:51.020
Between that and handicrafts and puzzles,

14:51.020 --> 14:54.530
you really do have patience for 
working with your hands, huh?

14:54.970 --> 14:56.760
No, this is important.

14:56.760 --> 15:00.250
Visualizing the goal can bring 
all our efforts together.

15:00.250 --> 15:02.410
Oh, man...

15:02.410 --> 15:03.850
What's this? A city?

15:03.850 --> 15:05.590
I'm interested in the superalloys!

15:05.590 --> 15:06.250
I want it!

15:06.800 --> 15:09.010
You have crazy hungry eyes.

15:09.460 --> 15:12.010
We're going to be digging up 
materials from all over the world.

15:12.370 --> 15:16.770
There's no way a few dozen of us 
on the <i>Perseus</i> are going to cut it.

15:17.030 --> 15:23.770
We're going to wake up statues everywhere 
and build new cities all over the world!

15:43.740 --> 15:46.130
Th-That's a bit ambitious, isn't it?

15:46.990 --> 15:48.650
But thanks to Treasure Island,

15:48.650 --> 15:50.890
we can make all the revival 
fluid we could ever need.

15:50.890 --> 15:52.550
This is no longer a hypothetical!

15:52.550 --> 15:56.930
We're finally going to save 
all seven billion humans, huh?

15:56.930 --> 15:58.720
Yeah, that's right.

15:58.720 --> 16:00.310
We're all building it together.

16:00.730 --> 16:04.560
We'll have each city around the 
world dig and collect and build...

16:13.350 --> 16:15.370
And we'll jet off of this planet!

16:33.160 --> 16:34.680
The one thing I'm worried about...

16:35.650 --> 16:39.190
is that once we start reviving 
people everywhere we go,

16:39.190 --> 16:42.140
we might hit the organizational 
limit that Gen was concerned about.

16:42.460 --> 16:44.090
Dunbar's number.

16:44.090 --> 16:45.600
One hundred fifty people.

16:46.140 --> 16:48.020
We'll be blowing way past that.

16:48.930 --> 16:50.230
He's right.

16:50.230 --> 16:53.740
There's going to be a lot of big-time 
baddies among those people.

16:55.070 --> 16:58.980
Though once social order is 
established in the new towns,

16:58.980 --> 17:01.910
everyone will accept it 
and bring about stability.

17:01.910 --> 17:03.580
Bootstrapping will be the risky part.

17:03.580 --> 17:06.950
Mm. But I suspect we'll never 
run into a situation

17:06.950 --> 17:09.690
where we need to deal 
with a rogue individual.

17:10.230 --> 17:10.880
It'll be fine.

17:11.960 --> 17:13.000
But...

17:14.570 --> 17:16.130
It'll be fine.

17:18.040 --> 17:19.260
Oh, you're right!

17:19.260 --> 17:20.560
It's totally fine!

17:20.560 --> 17:23.070
Tsuka-san's famous overseas, too.

17:23.070 --> 17:26.500
And anyone who doesn't know 
him will end up finding out.

17:26.500 --> 17:28.740
Tsukasa's way too powerful.

17:29.850 --> 17:33.830
Looks like we'll be circumnavigating 
the planet eastward.

17:34.560 --> 17:35.430
Good!

17:35.430 --> 17:37.850
A cross-Pacific voyage right from the start!

17:38.700 --> 17:39.770
It's all water?!

17:39.770 --> 17:41.580
That's pretty far.

17:41.580 --> 17:45.190
We're just like Columbus 
discovering the New World.

17:45.190 --> 17:50.680
The first one to discover land 
will be awarded 100,000 drago!

17:52.610 --> 17:53.960
Reward money?

17:53.960 --> 17:55.550
Drago?

17:57.110 --> 17:59.480
No, he means, er... Dora...emon!

17:59.480 --> 18:02.840
W-Wouldn't it be nice if we could build him?

18:04.580 --> 18:06.650
Ryusui, honey!

18:06.650 --> 18:08.820
Don't try to get close to Tsuka-san!

18:08.820 --> 18:10.610
It's dangerous! You two 
would never get along!

18:11.360 --> 18:15.400
Ryusui's absolutely an established 
power of the new world.

18:15.400 --> 18:18.010
Tsuka-san loathes that kind of stuff.

18:18.010 --> 18:20.990
Honestly, I don't...

18:26.950 --> 18:30.940
You weren't as bad as the rumors said, though.

18:33.390 --> 18:34.600
It's futile.

18:34.600 --> 18:39.260
No matter how much you 
may hate me, I love you.

18:40.640 --> 18:43.010
I love all women!

18:43.010 --> 18:44.460
That includes you.

18:44.460 --> 18:45.350
And men!

18:45.350 --> 18:46.770
I want everyone!

18:47.850 --> 18:50.350
Naturally, that includes Tsukasa, too.

18:51.030 --> 18:53.570
Y-You can't just control everyone with mon—

18:53.570 --> 18:56.730
Money is just a useful tool 
that we humans invented.

18:57.560 --> 19:00.570
Money doesn't exist to control people.

19:00.570 --> 19:02.570
It exists to bring desires together.

19:03.690 --> 19:06.160
It allows us to pool our strengths.

19:06.580 --> 19:10.120
That is the very reason 
humanity is so powerful.

19:10.120 --> 19:11.140
Am I right?

19:14.430 --> 19:15.670
Humankind...

19:16.920 --> 19:21.060
When all of humanity's strength is 
combined, the science that it creates...

19:22.410 --> 19:24.460
can take us to the Moon.

19:27.530 --> 19:32.270
So, anyway, we're waking up all of humanity.

19:32.700 --> 19:34.570
We're gonna need a ton of alcohol.

19:34.570 --> 19:36.690
A metric shit-ton of it.

19:36.690 --> 19:37.900
That's right.

19:37.900 --> 19:41.360
The revival fluid is mostly alcohol.

19:41.360 --> 19:44.240
We're going to be waking up a 
mountain of people, aren't we?

19:44.240 --> 19:49.740
No grape wine or potato 
wine is going to suffice.

19:49.740 --> 19:51.000
That's why...

19:52.940 --> 19:55.150
The first city we make is going to be...

19:59.630 --> 20:01.070
the city of corn.

20:05.130 --> 20:08.260
And it's going to be in the Americas.

20:06.300 --> 20:08.260
m 0 0 l 160 0 l 160 40 l 0 40

20:06.300 --> 20:08.260
Americas

20:09.220 --> 20:10.230
Corn?

20:10.570 --> 20:12.600
That's why you're in such a hurry.

20:12.600 --> 20:15.150
It'll die if we don't get there before winter.

20:15.150 --> 20:17.480
Do we get to have grilled corn?!

20:18.140 --> 20:20.270
It's called Yellow Dent.

20:20.270 --> 20:26.140
The US prided itself on this absurdly 
productive, OP cultivar of corn.

20:26.140 --> 20:28.530
Pump out alcohol with this stuff,

20:28.530 --> 20:32.120
and reviving all seven billion 
humans won't seem that far off.

20:32.360 --> 20:36.330
And that grilled corn will 
feed all those people, too.

20:36.330 --> 20:39.610
That's two birds with one stone 
for growing our population!

20:43.170 --> 20:46.080
Remember when Senku-chan, Chrome-chan, and I

20:46.560 --> 20:52.850
used a record to fool everyone and told 
that lie that's sure to send us to Hell?

20:52.850 --> 20:55.630
That lie about the US 
having been back already.

20:56.500 --> 21:00.630
I guess we're making it true before 
we even get a chance to go to Hell.

21:01.070 --> 21:02.780
With our own hands.

21:04.460 --> 21:05.610
Yup.

21:13.730 --> 21:14.860
Let's go!

21:14.860 --> 21:17.710
Time for our global city-building tour!

21:33.590 --> 21:37.060
Shit, this is getting me pumped!

21:37.700 --> 21:41.480
I'm gonna see the whole world for myself!

21:43.820 --> 21:46.990
This is our first step on 
the road map to the Moon.

21:48.820 --> 21:50.210
Yeah.

21:50.960 --> 21:52.210
We're...

21:54.050 --> 21:55.580
...going to the Moon.

22:02.770 --> 22:04.800
Immediately.

22:10.160 --> 22:13.170
This is gonna be exhilarating!

23:51.590 --> 23:54.950
<b>Final Season Confirmed</b>

23:54.950 --> 23:59.950
<b>This is a work of fiction, but the plants, 
